WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A missing sound can feel like a word you clearly heard.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In 1970, Richard Warren replaced part of a recorded word with noise.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Some listeners heard a complete word anyway.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
That's perception filling in a gap, not evidence that the sound was there.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
And it does not prove that a meditation recording can transform your brain.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the source. Try a free exercise. Decide what claims you trust.
